    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely correct to highlight the substantial barrier of regulatory compliance and bureaucratic red tape, which disproportionately burdens smaller organizations. Beyond market volatility, the complexity of navigating federal mandates and shifting legal frameworks forces startups to divert critical resources away from product development into safety and legal avoidance. While financial instability and competition play roles, many founders argue that the sheer administrative burden and risk of non-compliance are the most direct inhibitors to rapid innovation and scaling.",
      "source": "target",
